           F I L E   U N I T   A S S I G N M E N T S

             INPUT UNITS:
              INP FILE (MAIN INPUT)               50    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.inp                                                                
              ICS FILE (INITIAL CONDITIONS)       55    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.ics                                                                

             OUTPUT UNITS:
              SMY FILE (RUN SUMMARY)              80    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.smy                                                                
              LST FILE (GENERAL OUTPUT)           60    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.lst                                                                
              RST FILE (RESTART DATA)             66    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.rst                                                                
              NOD FILE (NODEWISE OUTPUT)          30    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.nod                                                                
              ELE FILE (VELOCITY OUTPUT)          40    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.ele                                                                
              OBS FILE (OBSERVATION OUTPUT) (     70)   ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.obs (BASE FILENAME)

              NAMES FOR OBS AND OBC FILES WILL BE GENERATED AUTOMATICALLY FROM THE BASE NAMES LISTED ABOVE AND SCHEDULE NAMES
              LISTED LATER IN THIS FILE.  UNIT NUMBERS ASSIGNED TO THESE FILES WILL BE THE FIRST AVAILABLE NUMBERS GREATER THAN
              OR EQUAL TO THE VALUES LISTED ABOVE IN PARENTHESES.




           S I M U L A T I O N   M O D E   O P T I O N S

           - ASSUME SATURATED FLOW ONLY
           - ASSUME STEADY-STATE FLOW FIELD CONSISTENT WITH INITIAL TEMPERATURE CONDITIONS
           - ASSUME STEADY-STATE TRANSPORT
           - COLD START - BEGIN NEW SIMULATION
           - STORE RESULTS AFTER EVERY     9999 TIME STEPS IN RESTART FILE AS BACKUP AND FOR USE IN A SIMULATION RESTART




           S I M U L A T I O N   C O N T R O L   N U M B E R S

            34907     NUMBER OF NODES IN FINITE-ELEMENT MESH
            34320     NUMBER OF ELEMENTS IN MESH

               91     EXACT NUMBER OF NODES IN MESH AT WHICH PRESSURE IS A SPECIFIED CONSTANT OR FUNCTION OF TIME
              540     EXACT NUMBER OF NODES IN MESH AT WHICH TEMPERATURE IS A SPECIFIED CONSTANT OR FUNCTION OF TIME

              521     EXACT NUMBER OF NODES AT WHICH FLUID INFLOW OR OUTFLOW IS A SPECIFIED CONSTANT OR FUNCTION OF TIME
             1637     EXACT NUMBER OF NODES AT WHICH A SOURCE OR SINK OF ENERGY IS A SPECIFIED CONSTANT OR FUNCTION OF TIME

             2381     EXACT NUMBER OF NODES AT WHICH PRESSURE AND TEMPERATURE WILL BE OBSERVED




           N U M E R I C A L   C O N T R O L   D A T A

                   0.00000     "UPSTREAM WEIGHTING" FACTOR
                1.0000E-02     SPECIFIED PRESSURE BOUNDARY CONDITION FACTOR
                1.0000E+02     SPECIFIED TEMPERATURE BOUNDARY CONDITION FACTOR
1



           T E M P O R A L   C O N T R O L   A N D   S O L U T I O N   C Y C L I N G   D A T A

             NOTE: BECAUSE FLOW AND TRANSPORT ARE STEADY-STATE, USER-DEFINED SCHEDULES ARE NOT IN EFFECT.  
             STEADY-STATE RESULTS WILL BE WRITTEN TO THE APPROPRIATE OUTPUT FILES.

             THE FOLLOWING 4 SCHEDULES CAN BE USED TO CONTROL SPECIFICATION OF STEADY-STATE BOUNDARY
             CONDITIONS IN (OPTIONAL) .BCS FILES:

                SCHEDULE TIME_STEPS   CONSISTS OF TIME STEPS 0 (STEADY FLOW) AND 1 (STEADY TRANSPORT);
                                         THIS SCHEDULE IS DEFINED AUTOMATICALLY BY SUTRA

                SCHEDULE STEPS_1&UP   IDENTICAL TO SCHEDULE "TIME_STEPS", EXCEPT THAT IT OMITS TIME STEP 0;
                                         THIS SCHEDULE IS DEFINED AUTOMATICALLY BY SUTRA

                SCHEDULE STEP_0       CONSISTS ONLY OF TIME STEP 0;
                                         THIS SCHEDULE IS DEFINED AUTOMATICALLY BY SUTRA

                SCHEDULE STEP_1       CONSISTS ONLY OF TIME STEP 1;
                                         THIS SCHEDULE IS DEFINED AUTOMATICALLY BY SUTRA

             SOLUTION CYCLING DATA:

                         1     FLOW SOLUTION CYCLE (IN TIME STEPS)
                         1     TRANSPORT SOLUTION CYCLE (IN TIME STEPS)

                FLOW AND TRANSPORT SOLUTIONS ARE ALSO COMPUTED AUTOMATICALLY ON TIME STEPS ON WHICH FLOW-RELATED 
                AND TRANSPORT-RELATED BOUNDARY CONDITIONS, RESPECTIVELY, ARE SET IN (OPTIONAL) BCS FILES.




           I T E R A T I O N   C O N T R O L   D A T A

             NON-ITERATIVE SOLUTION




           S O L V E R - R E L A T E D   P A R A M E T E R S

             SOLVER FOR P: IC-PRECONDITIONED CONJUGATE GRADIENT    

                      3000     MAXIMUM NUMBER OF MATRIX SOLVER ITERATIONS DURING P SOLUTION
                1.0000E-10     CONVERGENCE TOLERANCE FOR MATRIX SOLVER ITERATIONS DURING P SOLUTION

             SOLVER FOR U: ILU-PRECONDITIONED GMRES                

                       400     MAXIMUM NUMBER OF MATRIX SOLVER ITERATIONS DURING U SOLUTION
                1.0000E-12     CONVERGENCE TOLERANCE FOR MATRIX SOLVER ITERATIONS DURING U SOLUTION




           O U T P U T   C O N T R O L S   A N D   O P T I O N S

             .LST FILE
             ---------

                  -90   PRINTED OUTPUT CYCLE (IN TIME STEPS)

             - CANCEL PRINT OF NODE COORDINATES, THICKNESSES AND POROSITIES
             - CANCEL PRINT OF ELEMENT PERMEABILITIES AND DISPERSIVITIES
             - CANCEL PRINT OF NODE INCIDENCES IN EACH ELEMENT

             - PRINT PRESSURES AND SATURATIONS AT NODES ON EACH TIME STEP WITH OUTPUT
             - CALCULATE AND PRINT VELOCITIES AT ELEMENT CENTROIDS ON EACH TIME STEP WITH OUTPUT
             - PRINT TEMPERATURES AT NODES ON EACH TIME STEP WITH OUTPUT

             - CALCULATE AND PRINT FLUID AND ENERGY BUDGETS ON EACH TIME STEP WITH OUTPUT


             .NOD FILE
             ---------

                   90   PRINTED OUTPUT CYCLE (IN TIME STEPS)

             COLUMN 1:  X-COORDINATE             
             COLUMN 2:  Y-COORDINATE             
             COLUMN 3:  PRESSURE                 
             COLUMN 4:  CONCENTRATION/TEMPERATURE
             COLUMN 5:  SATURATION               


             .ELE FILE
             ---------

                   90   PRINTED OUTPUT CYCLE (IN TIME STEPS)

             COLUMN 1:  X-COORDINATE OF CENTROID 
             COLUMN 2:  Y-COORDINATE OF CENTROID 
             COLUMN 3:  X-VELOCITY               
             COLUMN 4:  Y-VELOCITY               


             .OBS AND .OBC FILES
             -------------------

             UNIT      70    ASSIGNED TO Case-170922a.obs                                                                

             NOTE: BECAUSE FLOW AND TRANSPORT ARE STEADY-STATE, USER-DEFINED SCHEDULES ARE NOT IN EFFECT.  
             STEADY-STATE OBSERVATIONS WILL BE WRITTEN TO THE APPROPRIATE OUTPUT FILES.




